.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-ROTATE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-rotate
.Nd say that a seal key was replaced by a new one
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis rotate
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl n Ar new
.Op Fl -new-pub Ar new.pub
.Op Fl -at Ar time
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl f
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis rotate
writes a key statement
.Pq Ql noqtis-keys-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5
that the signing key
.Ar key
was replaced by
.Ar new
from
.Ar time .
Both keys sign it: the old one to say so, the new one to show that its
holder has it.
Give the statement to those who check your capsules:
.Xr noqtis-check 1
.Fl p Ar key.pub
.Fl -keys Ar file
then accepts capsules sealed with
.Ar new ,
and capsules sealed with
.Ar key
only when a verified timestamp shows they were sealed before
.Ar time .
Rotate again from
.Ar new
to go on; the chain is followed up to 32 rotations.
.Pp
Each signature is checked before the statement is written.
Both keys must be post-quantum signature keys (ML-DSA, SLH-DSA or a
hybrid), of the same or of different algorithms.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k Ar key , Fl -key Ns = Ns Ar key
The secret key being replaced.
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
Its public key.
Default:
.Ar key Ns Pa .pub .
.It Fl n Ar new , Fl -new Ns = Ns Ar new
The secret key that replaces it.
.It Fl -new-pub Ar new.pub
Its public key.
Default:
.Ar new Ns Pa .pub .
.It Fl -at Ar time
When the replacement takes effect, as
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
(UTC, 1970 or later).
Default: now.
.It Fl -reason Ar text
Up to 255 bytes of text, kept in the statement.
.It Fl o Ar file , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar file
Write the statement to
.Ar file
instead of standard output.
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace
.Ar file
if it exists.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
The statement was written.
.It 2
A usage error, a key file that cannot be read, keys that are not a pair
or not post-quantum, the new key equal to the old one, or a file that
cannot be written.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-DSA-65 -o me2
$ noqtis rotate -k me -n me2 --reason "new laptop" -o me-me2.keys
$ noqtis seal -k me2 results
$ noqtis check -p me.pub --keys me-me2.keys results
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-revoke 1 ,
.Xr nqkstmt 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
